# Voron 2.611 — parse + MCU-load smoke under simulated MCUs.
# Run via: cd vendor/klipper && python scripts/test_klippy.py \
#           -d ../../tests/dict ../../tests/voron-2-611.test
#
# Requires Linux (Klipper's chelper uses Linux-only kernel headers).
# CI runs it on ubuntu-22.04 via .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# What this catches: config syntax errors, unknown sections, pin clashes
# across MCUs, unsupported sensor types (the LPC1769 temperature_mcu trap
# from PR #17), and jinja2 *parse* errors in macro bodies — i.e. everything
# that happens between `python klippy.py printer.cfg` and "Klipper ready".
#
# What this DOES NOT catch: gcode-execution behavior. We deliberately
# omit a smoke gcode sequence because test_klippy.py *does* execute
# commands (despite a previous comment here that claimed otherwise),
# and most of our macros touch probe state (G28 → safe_z_home → Eddy
# probe → freq→Z calibration polynomial) that doesn't exist in CI.
# Seeding the full SAVE_CONFIG block in CI would maintain a 100-line
# calibration fixture that drifts whenever the Pi is re-calibrated.
# Macro→macro reference rot is already covered by L2 (macro_refcheck);
# runtime gcode behavior is L6 (post-deploy smoke on real hardware).

CONFIG ../config/printer.cfg
DICTIONARY mcu.dict z=mcu.dict EBB=ebb-usb.dict eddy=eddy.dict mmu=easy-brd.dict
